        "I conclude that understanding Fichte\u2019s shift away from \u201cdeism,\u201d a species of what he would eventually call \u201cdogmatism,\u201d can also help us understand Fichte\u2019s critique of the latter kind of thinking and so shed light on Fichte\u2019s better-known views; and I emphasize that Fichte\u2019s transition from a strict rationalism to a form of Kantianism may be of interest not only to scholarship on Fichte and the period, but likewise to work on rationalism in contemporary metaphysics.",
        "Fichte\u2019s First Principle of Right.Michael Nance - 2021 - Fichte-Studien 49:248-266."
